0009 — SESSION HANDOFF
LEGAiSEE COMMANDCENTER KNOWLEDGE SYSTEM

Version: 1.0
Status: ACTIVE GOVERNANCE STANDARD
Scope: /commandcenter/governance/KnowledgeSystem/

1. PURPOSE

This document defines the structured method for preserving, transferring, and reconstructing system state between sessions.

Its purpose is to ensure:

uninterrupted system development continuity
lossless transfer of architectural state
deterministic resumption of work
elimination of context dependency on chat memory
stable long-term build progression
2. CORE PRINCIPLE

All system work MUST be resumable from a handoff artifact alone.

A valid session handoff MUST contain sufficient information to:

reconstruct current system state
continue build execution
identify next actionable file
preserve governance integrity

No reliance on external memory is permitted.

3. SESSION HANDOFF STRUCTURE

Every session handoff MUST include the following sections:

3.1 SYSTEM STATE SNAPSHOT

Defines current system condition:

Must include:

completed files
active subsystem being built
current folder context
last executed build step
3.2 BUILD POSITION

Defines exact position in sequence:

Must include:

current file number
next file to be created
pending dependencies

Example format:

Current: 0009_SESSION_HANDOFF.md
Next: 0010_*.md (to be defined)
3.3 ACTIVE SUBSYSTEM

Defines which Knowledge System branch is currently active.

Example:

Knowledge System Core Documentation Layer
Governance Extension Layer
Operational Protocol Layer

Only one active subsystem SHOULD be declared per session unless explicitly required.

3.4 COMPLETED ARTIFACTS LIST

Must include:

all previously created files in sequence order
brief identification of each file purpose

Example:

0004_DOCUMENT_STANDARD.md — formatting enforcement rules
0005_WRITING_STYLE_GUIDE.md — linguistic constraints
0006_NUMBERING_STANDARD.md — sequencing rules
0007_FOLDER_STRUCTURE.md — structural constraints
0008_RELATIONSHIP_MODEL.md — dependency semantics
3.5 SYSTEM DEPENDENCY CONTEXT

Must define:

what this session depends on (governance rules, prior files)
what must NOT be changed during continuation

This ensures continuity of constraints.

3.6 NEXT ACTION INSTRUCTION

Must explicitly define:

next file to be created
required scope of that file
any constraints that must be inherited

No ambiguity allowed.

4. CONTINUITY RULE

A session is considered VALID only if:

previous session state is fully captured
next action is explicitly defined
no architectural drift is introduced during continuation

If any condition fails → session is INVALID.

5. HANDOFF LOSS PREVENTION RULE

If session continuity is broken:

The system MUST:

reconstruct latest valid handoff
identify last valid file
resume strictly from next sequential number
avoid reinterpretation of previous architecture

No redesign is permitted during recovery.

6. GOVERNANCE BINDING RULE

All session handoffs are governed by:

0004_DOCUMENT_STANDARD.md (structure rules)
0005_WRITING_STYLE_GUIDE.md (language rules)
0006_NUMBERING_STANDARD.md (sequence rules)
0007_FOLDER_STRUCTURE.md (location rules)
0008_RELATIONSHIP_MODEL.md (dependency rules)

This document MUST NOT override those rules.

It only coordinates execution continuity.

7. SESSION RESUMPTION PROTOCOL

When resuming a system session, the following order MUST be used:

Load latest SESSION_HANDOFF
Verify completed artifacts list
Confirm numbering sequence integrity
Identify next file
Continue build without redesign
8. SYSTEM ROLE OF THIS DOCUMENT

This document functions as:

continuity engine for Knowledge System development
state reconstruction blueprint
deterministic resumption protocol
memory-independent execution stabilizer

It ensures the system can be paused and resumed without loss of structural integrity.

